nat44: 512-element worker handoff queues; clamp frame-queue trace

NAT44-EI and NAT44-ED hand packets between workers through frame queues
of NAT_FQ_NELTS_DEFAULT (64) elements. Each element carries the packets
of one enqueue call, which at low load is often a few dozen, so 64
elements absorb only about a thousand packets. With one busy LAN host all
sessions sit on one worker and the other worker hands over its whole RSS
share; line-rate bursts then overflow the queue while the receiving
worker wakes up or runs at a low clock (adaptive RX, intel_pstate
powersave), and the packets are dropped as "congestion drop" (TCP
retransmits). Raise the default to 512 (about 1.1 MB per queue and
thread). The size could already be raised through the API.

The frame-queue trace arrays hold FRAME_QUEUE_MAX_NELTS (64) entries but
the dequeue trace indexed them by the queue size, writing past them for
queues larger than 64. Clamp both indices.

--- a/src/plugins/nat/nat44-ed/nat44_ed.h
+++ b/src/plugins/nat/nat44-ed/nat44_ed.h
@@ -22,8 +22,11 @@
 
 #include <nat/lib/lib.h>
 
-/* default number of worker handoff frame queue elements */
-#define NAT_FQ_NELTS_DEFAULT 64
+/* default number of worker handoff frame queue elements; each element holds
+ * one enqueue call, often far fewer than VLIB_FRAME_SIZE packets, so 64
+ * overflows on line-rate bursts while the receiving worker wakes up or runs
+ * at a low clock */
+#define NAT_FQ_NELTS_DEFAULT 512
 
